42:**Motion findings:** motion instants — stem removal ≈1000–2000 ms · hand release ≈2000–2500 ms · press descent ≈3000–4000 ms (mid at F-3500) · reveal between 4000–4500 ms (the cutter's lift/flip is a stop-motion jump inside this interval; the slab is simply THERE at 4500) · gather ≈5000–6000 ms · bowl addition by 7000 ms. Holds — the stem-on state is evidenced AT CP1 (source 40.0 s) only; seg-rel 0–1000 ms is the prior episode (CP0), so any opening stem-on hold in the build is an ALLOCATION choice, not a census hold (jev-observe-exit charge 2, applied) · solo cushion ≈2500–3000 ms · slab on cutter ≈4500–5000 ms · final bowl state at 7000 ms. What changes between states: stem star present→absent (CP1→CP2) · hands present→absent (CP2→CP3) · grid absent→covering (CP3→CP4, the occlusion that carries the swap) · cushion→red-dice slab under the lifted cutter (CP4→F-4500) · slab on cutter→dice in hands→dice in bowl (CP5→CP7). The grid in CP4/F-4500 reads ≈7 columns × 6 rows of square cells with wooden side handles.
