15:### 1.1 Catalogue mechanics (read firsthand)
16:- Digest §T10 (39–46 s, clip clips/pincushion-grid.mp4 41–46 s): "A tomato-red pincushion is de-pinned (its pins read as the tomato's stem-points), set into a grid cutter, and pressed through; what emerges is a slab of translucent red cubes — diced tomato — gathered by hand and added to the molcajete. The transformation is performed by a real kitchen tool doing its real job; the substitution rides inside the press's occlusion." Why it works: "the tool's function is the argument — a grid cutter can only output cubes, so the output's identity is forced by the instrument."
18:- **Firsthand corrections to the digest prose (priced readings, binding on the build):** (1) The visible de-stemming is the removal of the green felt STEM STAR (census CP1→CP2), not pin removal — the pearl-head pins REMAIN in the cushion through the press (visible in CP3/CP4 through the grid cells); digest B5's "de-pinning … fumbled" prices the same beat's low legibility. The build implements stem-star removal + pins retained. (2) The emerged "translucent red cubes" are literally translucent RED DICE with white pips (ev/t044 + census CP5 viewed firsthand: 3×3 slab, two layers, white pips on every top face) — the dice read as diced tomato; the build renders pipped cubes with `pipStyle` CONFIG-bound (dice/plain), it does not render unmarked tomato cubes. (3) The clip file covers only 41–46 s; the full window was censused from the archived `source.mp4` (VP9 1920×1080, 100.894 s, ffprobe this run) — the archived source segment WAS watched in motion via the frame census below (this seat has no player; the census is the motion record, A10.3 form).
20:### 1.2 Evidence frames viewed firsthand
21:- ev/t041-pincushion-tomato.jpg (sha256 ddd91315…e695): red tomato-form pincushion held in left hand, pearl-head pins across its top, green string segment lines converging at the crown; right hand holds the just-removed green felt stem beside it; two spare pincushions (red, green) top-right on the wooden board.
22:- ev/t044-grid-press.jpg (sha256 654e7281…b7c): the grid cutter lying flat on the board, a neat 3×3 (two-layer) slab of translucent red dice with white pips sitting on the grid's centre; hands releasing the cutter's wooden handles. This is the POST-press reveal state, not the press in progress (its filename/prose in the digest implies the press; the census CP4/fine frames carry the actual press).
