1. **The CONFIG-derived companions execute, but the timing-swap receipts cover only two of the seven companions that move under the filed swap.** The supplied harness computes all 11 default companion instants. With `pressDurMs` changed from 1000 to 1600, it executes F-3500 at 2800 ms and CP4 at 3600 ms. The same change moves F-4500, CP5, F-5500, CP6 and CP7 by 600 ms, as derived from their `holdEnd`, `liftEnd` and `gatherStart` expressions. The swapped branch files no executions for those five predicates at their moved instants. The evidence that would clear A11 is the evaluated default and swapped instant and raw predicate result for each affected checkpoint. [Build record, completion own checks and receipt index](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/recreations/T233-tool-transformation-grid-press/build-record.md:142)
2. **The strengthened predicates execute in the supplied harness, but inherited receipts still omit required observations.** P7 enforces grid rest and reports observed and expected offsets of −76.5 px. The fixed probes and companions share the P3, P4 and P7 predicates. P11 requires an empty post-swap diff and reports state at 3124, 3125 and 3126 ms. The completion index nevertheless claims complete raw receipts for the inherited P assertions. P0 omits press progress and visible cube count, P2 omits stem opacity and press progress, P5 omits visible cube count and occluder opacity, and P8 omits the all-cube transit result. A12/A13 require those observations in the corresponding receipts. For P8, an observed count of cubes between their slab and bowl positions, alongside the total, would establish the predicate. [Binding plan §2.3](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-040-wave-37/item-T233-observe-plan.md) · [Completion receipts](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/recreations/T233-tool-transformation-grid-press/build-record.md:142)
3. **The two CONFIG census omissions are cured.** Both stroke keys have explicit entries and matching render reads. I independently counted 103 entries under the filed convention: 82 top-level entries after expanding the `palette` and `pins` containers, plus 18 palette members and three pin member names. The construction record describes generated SVG geometry and CONFIG-driven state. The purity receipt records zero specimen hits. [CONFIG census §§2 and 4](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/recreations/T233-tool-transformation-grid-press/config-census.md:14) · [Render sites](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/recreations/T233-tool-transformation-grid-press/recreation.html:169)
4. **The tool-label vertical accounting is cured at the stated proxy scope.** I reproduced the baseline-relative PIL ink box for `GRID PRESS` at 28 px and sampled the unchanged build’s state at integer milliseconds. The 20 px ink box is fully inside the stage from 2625 through 3392 ms. At press bottom, the measured proxy interval is y=48–68 on the 400 px stage, yielding 48 px top clearance and 332 px bottom clearance. [Fit table, vertical accounting](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/recreations/T233-tool-transformation-grid-press/fit-table.md:15)
5. **The fidelity plan names its departures.** It implements stem-star removal with pins retained, the covered substitution, pipped dice and the gather into the bowl. It explicitly defers the prior-episode tail, hands and spare props, compresses the separate bowl shot, and substitutes a staggered reveal for the source jump. [Observe §1.1 and Plan §2.2](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-040-wave-37/item-T233-observe-plan.md:69)

